   "updated": 1735689600000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "- Each wall is a different system with its own deny (red boxes); a denial stops the call and leaves a log\n  row.\n- The user's own identity reaches the data plane: T2 goes in, T4 comes out, so Azure RBAC decides on\n  Wes, not on the server.\n- One request id (x-abw-request-id) ties the APIM, MCP and Storage rows; Entra and the guardrail use\n  other ids (diagram 09).",
   "fontSize": 18,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "originalText": "- Each wall is a different system with its own deny (red boxes); a denial stops the call and leaves a log\n  row.\n- The user's own identity reaches the data plane: T2 goes in, T4 comes out, so Azure RBAC decides on\n  Wes, not on the server.\n- One request id (x-abw-request-id) ties the APIM, MCP and Storage rows; Entra and the guardrail use\n  other ids (diagram 09).",
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "d03_0149",
